SaaS 0.6.5 singing-submarine - release notes
=============================================

New
---
* Scrubbing: hold next/prev (buttons 0.5 s, or n/p and the arrow keys) to
  seek through the song instead of skipping a pile of tracks. Steps grow the
  longer you hold (2 s, 5 s, 15 s); line 2 shows "» 1:23 / 4:56". It stops
  1 s before the end and never skips the track.
* LMS (Lyrion Music Server) as a network source: the server's music folder
  like a stick (view = "folders", the default) or its album list
  (view = "albums"). Works with LMS password protection.
* --test-network: checks every [[network]] server in the config (connect,
  folders, tags, stream) and says OK or what failed.
* The update file on the stick is now DLP6/Update/UPDATE4SAAS.pub.
  DLP6/Update/saas.pub keeps working.
* These notes: install.sh prints them after an upgrade, and
  python3 /opt/saas/main.py --notes prints them again.
* Jellyfin: API calls send the full MediaBrowser Authorization header (the
  form Jellyfin 12 keeps supporting).

Changed
-------
* next/prev buttons are now short/long buttons: a short press acts when you
  let go, holding scrubs. To get the old press-to-skip back, set e.g.
  next = { pin = 27, hold = false }
* Keyboard: a single tap of next/prev acts after your terminal's auto-repeat
  delay (~0.3-0.7 s). That's how a tap is told apart from a hold.

Recommended (nothing is forced, everything old still works)
-----------------------------------------------------------
1. If you updated over a stick: run the installer once as root, so the system
   parts match this version (rollback tool, and from 0.6.4 the power-off
   rule and config permissions):
       su -c '/opt/saas/package/install.sh --offline'
   (Afterwards saas-rollback can't undo the update anymore - do it once
   0.6.5 plays fine.)
2. Name update files UPDATE4SAAS.pub from now on. If your config has
   file = "DLP6/Update/saas.pub" under [update], you can change it to
   "DLP6/Update/UPDATE4SAAS.pub" (both names are looked for either way).
3. Using LMS? Add it to /etc/saas/config.toml (example: config/pi.toml in
   the release, /opt/saas/package/config/pi.toml after a stick update), then
   check it as root (the config is only readable for root and saas):
       su -c 'python3 /opt/saas/main.py -c /etc/saas/config.toml --test-network'
   The same command also checks your Jellyfin / Navidrome / DLNA entries.
